.TH CY 1 "" "camayoc" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cy, camayoc \- record and recall typed agent memory in a Quipu store
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cy record
.I entity
[\fB\-\-field\fR \fIvalue\fR ...]
.br
.B cy recall
.I entity
[\fIfilters\fR]
.br
.B cy topic add
.I name
.br
.B cy flush | cy mcp | cy prime
.SH DESCRIPTION
One purpose\-built command per memory entity. Every write goes through Quipu\(aqs SHACL shapes; a refusal names the missing field in plain words and exits 2.
.SH ENTITIES
.SS decision
Record one ruling on a scoped question: what was chosen, by whom, about what.
.TP
\fB\-\-chose\fR (required)
What was chosen, in one sentence.
.TP
\fB\-\-by\fR (required)
Who ruled: a Person or agent entity (IRI or local name).
.TP
\fB\-\-about\fR (required)
The entity the decision is about: host, repo, service, role, agent or person (IRI or local name).
.TP
\fB\-\-topic\fR (required)
The registered memory topic the decision answers (cy topic add registers one).
.TP
\fB\-\-over\fR (repeatable)
An alternative that was not chosen; repeat for each.
.TP
\fB\-\-rationale\fR
Why, in one or two sentences.
.TP
\fB\-\-decided\-in\fR
The board item or session the decision was made in (IRI or local name).
.TP
\fB\-\-verbatim\fR
The ruling in the decider\(aqs own words.
.SS directive
Record a standing rule: one imperative sentence, who issued it, who it binds.
.TP
\fB\-\-rule\fR (required)
The rule, as one imperative sentence.
.TP
\fB\-\-issued\-by\fR (required)
Who issued the rule: a Person or agent entity (IRI or local name).
.TP
\fB\-\-applies\-to\fR (required)
Who or what the rule binds: an agent, CrewRole or repo, or \(aqcrew\(aq for everyone.
.TP
\fB\-\-topic\fR (required)
The registered memory topic the rule governs (cy topic add registers one).
.TP
\fB\-\-issued\-on\fR
The date the rule was given, YYYY\-MM\-DD.
.TP
\fB\-\-why\fR
Why the rule exists, in one sentence.
.TP
\fB\-\-verbatim\fR
The rule in the issuer\(aqs own words.
.SS handoff
Write the agent\(aqs one current handoff; each write supersedes the last.
.TP
\fB\-\-agent\fR (required)
The agent the handoff is for (IRI or local name).
.TP
\fB\-\-next\fR (required) (repeatable)
A next step pointing at a board item, PR or entity; repeat, 1 to 7.
.TP
\fB\-\-waiting\-on\fR (repeatable)
What an item waits on; repeat, at most 7.
.TP
\fB\-\-context\fR (repeatable)
Context the next session needs; repeat, at most 3 lines.
.SS preference
Record how a person wants something done, in one context.
.TP
\fB\-\-person\fR (required)
Whose preference it is: a Person entity (IRI or local name).
.TP
\fB\-\-prefers\fR (required)
What the person prefers, in one sentence.
.TP
\fB\-\-context\fR (required)
Where it applies: email, chat, code\-review, document, artifact, form or travel.
.TP
\fB\-\-topic\fR (required)
The registered memory topic (cy topic add registers one).
.TP
\fB\-\-not\-when\fR
When the preference does not apply.
.TP
\fB\-\-example\fR
One short example of the preference applied.
.TP
\fB\-\-verbatim\fR
The preference in the person\(aqs own words.
.SS reference
Record where a system lives and how to reach it. Key names only, never secrets.
.TP
\fB\-\-subject\fR (required)
The system the reference points into: host, service, repo or tool (IRI or local name).
.TP
\fB\-\-topic\fR (required)
What the reference is for: a registered memory topic (cy topic add registers one).
.TP
\fB\-\-locator\fR (required)
Where it is: a URL, path, command or graph IRI. Never a secret.
.TP
\fB\-\-secret\-ref\fR
The secret\-store key name that holds the credential. A key name, never a value.
.TP
\fB\-\-access\fR
How to authenticate, in one sentence, without the secret.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B QUIPU_SERVER
Quipu base URL (default http://localhost:3030).
.TP
.B QUIPU_AUTH_TOKEN, QUIPU_AUTH_TOKEN_FILE
Bearer for writes, else ~/.config/quipu/token. Never printed.
.TP
.B SHANTY_AGENT
The agent recorded as recordedBy.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 recorded, unchanged, superseded or queued; 2 refused; 3 Quipu error.
.SH SEE ALSO
cy prime; docs/design/agent\-memory\-entities.md in the camayoc repository.
